  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PPDP 2.0 - MSD for Inclusive Decent Employment and Productive Livelihoods - PPDP Inclusive Productive Employment &amp; Livelihoods - an MSD approach</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">PPDP 2.0 - MSD for Inclusive Decent Employment and Productive Livelihoods</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen &#xE4;r en forts&#xE4;ttning p&#xE5; st&#xF6;det till Inclusive Economic Growth through Decent Work in the Great Rift Valley (insats nr 10305). Den &#xE4;r en sk Public Private Development Partnership som genomf&#xF6;rs av ILO i samarbete med ForumCiv samt privata och offentliga akt&#xF6;rer i Narok, Nakuru och Kajiado l&#xE4;n. Insatsen syftar till att skapa f&#xF6;ruts&#xE4;ttningar f&#xF6;r &#xF6;kade och f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttrade arbets- och f&#xF6;rs&#xF6;rjningsm&#xF6;jligheter med anst&#xE4;ndiga arbetsvillkor. Stort fokus ska l&#xE4;ggas p&#xE5; den gr&#xF6;na omst&#xE4;llningen, j&#xE4;mst&#xE4;lldhet och SRHR. Erfarenheter, l&#xE4;rdomar och best practices fr&#xE5;n f&#xF6;rsta fasen ska skalas upp genom att st&#xF6;det antar en Market Systems Development-ansats.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The contribution is a continuation of the PPDP for Inclusive Economic Growth through Decent Work in the Great Rift Valley (contribution no 10305). This PPDP 2.0 will be implemented by ILO in close collaboration with ForumCiv and together with public and private actors in Narok, Nakuru and Kajiado counties. It aims at increased job creation and improved conditions for job opportunities, self employment and livelihoods. Great focus will be given to the green transition, gender equality and SRHR. Experiences, lessons learned and best practices from the first phase will be scaled up by applying a Market Systems Development (MSD) Approach to the project implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overarching aim of the project is to contribute to the inclusive and sustainable socio-economic development in the Great Rift Valley, with the overall development objective being to promote the creation of inclusive productive employment and livelihoods.

To contribute to these overall objectives, the specific objectives for the programme are the following outcomes:  

- enhanced employability and job access through vocational education and skills development;

- growing sustainable enterprises and value chains for increased inclusive job opportunities; and

- improved opportunities for inclusive and productive employment and sustainable livelihoods at community level through enhanced community engagement.</narrative>
  </description>
